  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The proposed residual resembles established combinations of long-term sequence features and short-term item pooling. Originality and expected benefit need comparison with these methods and a simple recent-item scoring baseline.",
    "Implementation remains underspecified: embedding scaling, normalization placement, empty-prefix handling, padding behavior, and category-specific gates can affect results. A sigmoid gate initialized at -4 may learn slowly. Shared input/output embeddings also allow the intervention to change candidate representations, complicating attribution to recency.",
    "The evaluation plan lacks a compute allocation within 43,200 GPU-seconds and a fixed checkpoint-selection rule. Perturbation controls need precise masking semantics and paired sampling. One training seed cannot establish training robustness, and repeated validation selection introduces uncertainty beyond paired user bootstrap intervals."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Establish relevant prior art and identify inexpensive controls that distinguish temporal gains from simple item similarity.",
      "query": "How do FPMC, Fossil, and SASRec extensions combine recent-item embeddings with longer-term user representations? What ablations distinguish benefits of a gated five-item mean residual from last-item similarity, ungated recent-item pooling, and ordinary SASRec?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve architecture details that could undermine reproducibility or make the proposed gate ineffective.",
      "query": "For sequential recommenders with tied input and output item embeddings, what are the effects of adding a LayerNorm-normalized recent-history residual after the encoder? Examine embedding-scale mismatch, sigmoid gates initialized near zero, gradient flow, causal pooling with padding, and tests for training-inference score parity."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make the diagnostic and selection design interpretable under the fixed benchmark and limited search budget.",
      "query": "What established protocols support frozen sequential-recommender recency audits using matched recent versus old-item masking while controlling for final-item identity, positional shifts, and out-of-distribution padding? How should paired sampled HR@10 comparisons distinguish user-bootstrap uncertainty, training-seed variation, and adaptive validation selection?"
    }
  ]
}
